---
/**
 * What it costs to find out what every dial should do, plotted two ways.
 *
 * The teaching load is carried by the two slopes and by the sentences attached
 * to them, not by the two colours: one line is solid and climbs, the other is
 * dashed and stays flat, and each says in words what it is. Strip the colour
 * out and both survive (hard rule 9). The marks on the six-dial machine are a
 * circle and a square for the same reason.
 *
 * The three counts along the bottom are the ones `BlameFlow/logic.ts` computes
 * and `logic.test.ts` pins, so this diagram cannot drift away from the machine
 * the reader is about to use.
 *
 * Decorative by itself, so `aria-hidden`: `Figure` supplies the accessible name
 * and the description.
 */
---

<svg viewBox="0 0 640 344" class="w-full" aria-hidden="true">
  <!-- Axes. Neither carries numbers: the shape of the two lines is the point,
       and a scale that reaches seventy billion has no honest tick marks. -->
  <g class="stroke-rule-strong" stroke-width="1.25">
    <line x1="100" y1="250" x2="580" y2="250"></line>
    <line x1="100" y1="55" x2="100" y2="250"></line>
    <line x1="170" y1="250" x2="170" y2="257"></line>
  </g>

  <!-- One extra run of the whole machine for every dial in it. -->
  <line
    x1="100"
    y1="244"
    x2="545"
    y2="62"
    class="stroke-accent"
    stroke-width="2"></line>

  <g transform="rotate(-22.2 322.5 153)">
    <text x="322.5" y="138" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-ink" font-size="10"
      >nudge one dial, run the whole machine again —</text
    >
    <text x="322.5" y="150" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-ink" font-size="10"
      >once more for every dial there is</text
    >
  </g>

  <!-- One forward run and one sweep back, whatever the machine is. -->
  <line
    x1="100"
    y1="244"
    x2="580"
    y2="244"
    class="stroke-accent-2"
    stroke-width="2"
    stroke-dasharray="6 4"></line>

  <g class="fill-ink" font-size="10">
    <text x="572" y="216" text-anchor="end"
      >one forward run and one sweep back —</text
    >
    <text x="572" y="229" text-anchor="end"
      >the same two runs however many dials there are</text
    >
  </g>

  <!-- Where the machine in the instrument below sits on each line. Circle and
       square, so the two are told apart without colour. -->
  <circle cx="170" cy="215" r="4.5" class="fill-ink"></circle>
  <rect x="166" y="240" width="8" height="8" class="fill-ink"></rect>

  <text
    x="170"
    y="272"
    text-anchor="middle"
    class="fill-ink-muted"
    font-size="10">the six-dial machine below</text
  >

  <text
    x="340"
    y="292"
    text-anchor="middle"
    class="fill-ink-faint"
    font-size="10">how many dials the machine has →</text
  >

  <text
    x="34"
    y="152"
    text-anchor="middle"
    transform="rotate(-90 34 152)"
    class="fill-ink-faint"
    font-size="10">full runs of the machine needed</text
  >

  <g class="fill-ink-muted" font-size="11">
    <text x="8" y="318"
      >That six-dial machine takes 6 multiplications to run forwards and 8 to
      sweep the blame back.</text
    >
    <text x="8" y="334"
      >Getting the same six numbers by nudging each dial takes 42, and that gap
      widens with every dial added.</text
    >
  </g>
</svg>
